---
import Slide from '../ui/Slide.astro';
import Callout from '../ui/Callout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../ui/CodeBlock.astro';
import Pill from '../ui/Pill.astro';
---

<Slide
  id="s19b-layer-scheduling-commands"
  chapter="Layers"
  title="Scheduling — Commands"
  notes="describe pod Events for FailedScheduling. Check node taints and top nodes if metrics-server installed. Myth: Pending always means not enough CPU — taints, affinity, PVC binding, and ResourceQuota block without touching CPU graphs."
>
  <div class="stagger flex flex-col gap-6">
    <section>
      <h3 class="mb-3 font-display text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-deck-cyan">Typical commands</h3>
      <CodeBlock
        lang="bash"
        caption="Why Pending?"
        code={`kubectl describe pod <pod> -n <ns>   # Events: FailedScheduling
kubectl get events -n <ns> --field-selector involvedObject.name=<pod>
kubectl describe nodes | grep -A5 Taints
kubectl top nodes   # if metrics-server installed`}
      />
    </section>

    <Callout type="myth">
      Pending always means not enough CPU. Taints, affinity, PVC binding, and ResourceQuota block scheduling without touching CPU graphs.
    </Callout>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 border-t border-deck-border/60 pt-4">
      <Pill tone="amber">Decision hint</Pill>
      <span class="text-lg text-deck-muted">Copy the FailedScheduling reason — it usually names the fix.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</Slide>
